Modelica source:
```modelica
connector HeatPort
  Real T;
  flow Real Q_flow;
end HeatPort;
model Capacity
  HeatPort port;
end Capacity;
model Conduction
  HeatPort port_a;
  HeatPort port_b;
end Conduction;
model Convection
  HeatPort solid;
  HeatPort fluid;
end Convection;
model Study
  Capacity windingLosses;
  Capacity coreLosses;
  Capacity winding;
  Capacity core;
  Capacity Twinding;
  Capacity Tcore;
  Capacity environment;
  Conduction winding2core;
  Convection convection;
equation
  connect(windingLosses.port, winding.port);
  connect(coreLosses.port, core.port);
  connect(winding.port, winding2core.port_a);
  connect(winding2core.port_b, core.port);
  connect(winding.port, Twinding.port);
  connect(core.port, Tcore.port);
  connect(winding2core.port_b, convection.solid);
  connect(convection.fluid, environment.port);
end Study;
```

Question:
Return the canonical signed member vector for the primitive flow connection set containing core.port.Q_flow.

Target:
core.port.Q_flow

Answer format:
Use ascending path:integer entries joined by commas without spaces; coefficients must be primitive, nonzero, and oriented so the first coefficient is positive.
